Build a phone's password pages: the shell's side of chrome://password-manager.

A phone draws its own password list, detail and edit pages, and asks the
engine for what they show and do -- the list without secrets, and, inside the
window the shell's own verification opened, the plain text, edits, deletion
and CSV export. That lives in chrome/browser/ui/ohos/shell_passwords_ohos.cc,
an overlay file; this only adds it to the build next to the other shell
files.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after ohos-shell-extensions-page.patch.

